-- title:
--   Lengths multiply along an injective map from a DVR
-- statement:
--   Let $D$ be a commutative ring that is an integral domain and a discrete valuation ring, and let $L$ be a commutative ring that is an integral domain and local. Let $\varphi : D \to L$ be a ring homomorphism which is injective as a function, and let $f \in D$ be nonzero. Then the equality
--   $$\operatorname{length}_L\bigl(L/\varphi(f)L\bigr) \;=\; \operatorname{length}_D\bigl(D/fD\bigr)\cdot\operatorname{length}_L\bigl(L/\varphi(\mathfrak m_D)L\bigr)$$
--   holds, where $\mathfrak m_D$ is the maximal ideal of $D$, $\varphi(f)L$ and $fD$ denote the ideals generated by the single elements $\varphi(f)$ and $f$, $\varphi(\mathfrak m_D)L$ denotes the ideal of $L$ generated by the image of $\mathfrak m_D$ under $\varphi$, and the lengths are `Module.length` of the indicated cyclic quotient modules, taken over $D$ and over $L$ respectively. The equality is an identity in the extended natural numbers, so it also covers the cases in which one of the factors on the right is infinite; in particular, when $\varphi$ carries a uniformiser of $D$ to a unit of $L$ both sides are zero.
--
--   This is the multiplicativity of length along an injective homomorphism from a discrete valuation ring into a local domain: the length of $L/\varphi(f)L$ is the valuation $\operatorname{ord}_D(f)$ multiplied by the local ramification invariant $\operatorname{length}_L(L/\varphi(\mathfrak m_D)L)$. It is used in the local study of the crossing models at the nodes of modular curves, where the multiplicity of a node-ring element at a branch is computed as its order at the relevant height-one prime times the length attached to that branch.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsDiscreteValuationRing_length_quotient_map_span_eq_length_mul_length.lean

